WEBVTT

00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:22.360
Speaker 1: You see, one thing that happens to a lot of people, or at least I think, let me put it this way.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:41.130
Speaker 1: I've heard a lot of cases of people who had medical conditions that were very treatable and conditions that could have been nipped by the bud if there was an early diagnosis, but somehow they just went on until things escalated.

00:00:41.609 --> 00:00:48.650
Speaker 1: You see, when we talk about the place of prayer, a lot of people don't really understand that this is what happens.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.970
Speaker 1: Part of what I'm going to share tomorrow is that prayer has a cumulative effect.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.690
Speaker 1: If you've been following me, you know that already.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:55.810
Speaker 1: You know that already.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:02.850
Speaker 1: Prayer has a cumulative effect and it's vice versa.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:14.250
Speaker 1: The same way, if you are not praying daily, it also has a gradual but sure deteriorative effect.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.650
Speaker 1: Let me put it that way.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:28.670
Speaker 1: If there's an expression like that, and we have these five firefighting approach to the things of God, where until things are really bad, that's when we know there's a problem.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.630
Speaker 1: What if your alarm goes off at the right time?

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:43.390
Speaker 1: What if your alarm goes off not when the house is already burnt to ashes, but just when the fire is beginning to loom and you can just extinguish it?

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.750
Speaker 1: Just what if?

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:51.080
Speaker 1: Because you see, a lot of people do not even know when they are in trouble spiritually.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.160
Speaker 1: If you can go three days without prayer, See, let me tell you something.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:01.440
Speaker 1: There are some things that when I see, I know that you'll be in trouble.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.360
Speaker 1: It's just a matter of time.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.880
Speaker 1: It doesn't matter how fine you look right now, you are in trouble.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.680
Speaker 1: You're already in trouble.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:16.600
Speaker 1: If the devil can get you to a place where you can conveniently go three days without praying.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.100
Speaker 1: Or guess what?

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.180
Speaker 1: Now this is the part a lot of people don't know.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.300
Speaker 1: You pray.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:21.780
Speaker 1: But.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.420
Speaker 1: If you get this expression, it's been long since you warmed your heart.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:40.020
Speaker 1: Just imagine someone, you have food you're trying to preserve, and you put it on the fire, but it's not warmed, and you take it off.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.660
Speaker 1: And you, I mean now you say, oh, there was fire.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.440
Speaker 1: The food is still going to get bad.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.200
Speaker 1: Do you understand?

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.360
Speaker 1: See, you must warm your heart, warm your soul every day.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:05.000
Speaker 1: If your soul is not warmed, if your spirit is not warmed, It's only a matter of time.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.880
Speaker 1: It's only a matter of time.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.680
Speaker 1: And that's why you see a lot of Christians.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.520
Speaker 1: They are Christians, but their experience is not different from the world.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:26.120
Speaker 1: When you see a Christian that a witch can successfully put a hex on, that's why, because when they look at you see in the realm of the Spirit.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:33.720
Speaker 1: And you don't take this with a pinch of salt because it's not necessarily doctrine.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.120
Speaker 1: It's just spiritual experience of spiritual gifts.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.360
Speaker 1: In the realm of the Spirit.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:57.670
Speaker 1: Your energy levels show based on how sincere your walk with God is and how much you have blocked off contradictions in your, in your moral life and how vibrant your prayer life is.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:03:59.910
Speaker 1: Your energy levels show.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.110
Speaker 1: And so it's.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:05.500
Speaker 1: They're able to see people who are vulnerable.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.050
Speaker 1: And so listen to me.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:20.450
Speaker 1: Every passing day that you don't pray, it's not about whether there is a problem or not.

00:04:21.089 --> 00:04:22.050
Speaker 1: There will be problem.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:28.450
Speaker 1: And so Jesus doesn't only tell us why we must pray.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.570
Speaker 1: He tells us what will happen if we don't.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.050
Speaker 1: Men ought always to pray, not to faint.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:37.410
Speaker 1: It means if you're not praying, you are vulnerable, you're going to faint.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:46.290
Speaker 1: It means there might be situations that you will not have the capacity to handle.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:50.530
Speaker 1: All right, that's just what, that's what is going to happen.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.090
Speaker 1: Pray that you do not fall into temptation.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.090
Speaker 1: He tells you what will.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.690
Speaker 1: Will happen if you don't pray.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.770
Speaker 1: You will fall into temptation.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:04:59.730
Speaker 1: It doesn't matter how.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.770
Speaker 1: How many consonants are in your tongues.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.610
Speaker 1: Yeah, you will fall into temptation.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:05.890
Speaker 1: He tells you what will happen.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:12.210
Speaker 1: So let your alarm go off at the right time, not when you're already struggling.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.209
Speaker 1: Now you have from nowhere, a new habit has showed up.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.010
Speaker 1: Do you know what it is?

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.810
Speaker 1: It's better to nip these things by the board early.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:30.970
Speaker 1: So create a discipline where it's not about if there's trouble or not.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:36.570
Speaker 1: If you go a day without praying, you must never break your streak.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:39.610
Speaker 1: You know, I told you last week, never break your streak.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:41.290
Speaker 1: Never break your streak.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.210
Speaker 1: Never break your prayer streak.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.290
Speaker 1: Never break your prayer streak.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:45.810
Speaker 1: Never.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:48.490
Speaker 1: And in fact, this is the one a lot of people struggle with.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.730
Speaker 1: Don't break your study streak.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.610
Speaker 1: Don't break your study streak.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:55.140
Speaker 1: Just.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:08.860
Speaker 1: You see, a lot of us, the problem is we outgrew devotion, family devotion, personal devotion, personal study, even devotionals.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.700
Speaker 1: We say it's too elementary.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.620
Speaker 1: It's for upcoming now.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:13.700
Speaker 1: How you doing now?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.380
Speaker 1: So well, how you doing?

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.700
Speaker 1: How's it going for you?

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:32.050
Speaker 1: So what if no matter how boring you subjected yourself to the boredom of consistency every day the fire will not go out?

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.930
Speaker 1: That is, therein lies your safety.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:51.910
Speaker 1: You see, a lot of people know about prayer, for healing, for miracles, and for whatever other reason there is something that prayer does well established in the world word of God that we don't see and that is this, that prayer strengthens your faith.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:57.590
Speaker 1: It strengthens your faith to the degree that if you don't pray, you're getting vulnerable.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:15.280
Speaker 1: And so when Jude is talking about people who crept in the church and deceived many people, he now says in verse 17, the book of Jude, but you, beloved, remember the words which were spoken before of the apostles of Jesus Christ, how that they told you that there will be mockers in the last time, who.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:23.190
Speaker 1: Who will walk according to ungodly lusts, These essential persons who cause divisions, having not the spirit, he says, but you, beloved.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:29.270
Speaker 1: But you, beloved, meaning you want to be saved from error.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:36.390
Speaker 1: He says, but you, beloved, building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Ghost, keep yourself in the love of God.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.990
Speaker 1: For some reason, the Charismatic church focuses on verse 20.

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:41.760
Speaker 1: The focus on what?

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.280
Speaker 1: They don't focus on why.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.960
Speaker 1: It tells you that praying in the Holy Ghost will keep you in the love of God.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.120
Speaker 1: That's what prayer does.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.160
Speaker 1: That's what prayer does.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.280
Speaker 1: It just renews your spiritual energy and vigor.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.520
Speaker 1: It gives you the fortitude to forge ahead.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:11.330
Speaker 1: And this is why Jesus will say to Simon, the devil has asked of you that he may sift you as wheat.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:14.810
Speaker 1: He says, but I've prayed for you that your faith will not fail.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:19.370
Speaker 1: You see, prayer is a strategy for preserving faith.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:24.090
Speaker 1: Listen, if you come to a point, let me give you a simple example.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:32.010
Speaker 1: If you ever come to a point where you're no longer sure that God heals, you're not praying.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:36.948
Speaker 1: You see, faith is not just, oh, I read it in a book.

00:08:37.589 --> 00:08:45.269
Speaker 1: There is something about prayer that strengthens your conviction about what you know that God can do.

00:08:46.629 --> 00:08:50.789
Speaker 1: If you don't have a prayer life, it doesn't matter what you read, you may not believe it.

00:08:50.789 --> 00:08:54.069
Speaker 1: I'm telling you, prayer strengthens your faith.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:08:59.360
Speaker 1: All right.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.040
Speaker 1: You know that text we always quote, resist devil and will flee from you.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.840
Speaker 1: Now Listen, it says, First Peter, Chapter 5, 8.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:15.520
Speaker 1: It says, Be sober, be vigilant, because your adversary, the devil walks about like a roaring lion seeking whom to devour.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:22.800
Speaker 1: He says, resist him steadfast in the faith, knowing that the same sufferings are experienced by your brotherhood in the world.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.760
Speaker 1: He says, resisting how?

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.160
Speaker 1: By being steadfast in the faith.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:32.760
Speaker 1: So steadfastness in the faith is what the devil is after.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:35.600
Speaker 1: Listen.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.520
Speaker 1: Listen to me.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:40.440
Speaker 1: When you are steadfast in the faith, you are resisting the devil.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:46.640
Speaker 1: When you are steadfast in the faith, when you resist the devil by steadfastness in the faith.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.920
Speaker 1: You won't have to resist him by some warfare.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.440
Speaker 1: Some warfare is unnecessary.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:54.890
Speaker 1: Some warfare is on account of the fact that you gave him a foothold in the first place.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.570
Speaker 1: Do you get what I'm saying?

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.010
Speaker 1: This is important.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:00.570
Speaker 1: Just be serious.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.330
Speaker 1: Every day, just be serious.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:15.850
Speaker 1: The simple things I can tell you if you keep a prayer time of one hour, even if it's 30 minutes, but it's vibrant and it's, oh, my God.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.220
Speaker 1: It will save you from a lot of emergencies.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:20.340
Speaker 1: It will.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:22.020
Speaker 1: It will.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:27.420
Speaker 1: And so how does this have to do with building a culture of prayer?

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:28.980
Speaker 1: I will tell you very simply.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:39.300
Speaker 1: When you know that if you don't pray, there will be consequences, maybe that will be incentive to pray.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:45.040
Speaker 1: When you know that the enemy is always looking for advantage.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.560
Speaker 1: He's literally looking for whom to devour.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.200
Speaker 1: He's looking for advantage.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.360
Speaker 1: You don't want to give him advantage.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.440
Speaker 1: That's why Paul said, let Satan have advantage.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.720
Speaker 1: Don't give him advantage.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.400
Speaker 1: So you know why I'm going to pray even when I don't feel like praying.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.200
Speaker 1: I don't want to give the devil advantage.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:22.210
Speaker 1: Sam.
